+  "phase": "REVIEW",
+  "input_package_sha256": "64a7882bc365b7305d771260560be6d5c1a6fcc1add65474546bf2a1fc7145d2",
+  "source_path": "02-Documentation/DocumentIdentity/04-Reference/DF-DID-012 - Document Identity Best Practices.md",
+  "source_sha256": "692230e6c874ddd97e8215334534b61c12b487e7e2a9ea85b9ac506513cd8c8e",
+  "source_bytes": 9231,
+  "source_lines_normalized": 317,
+  "source_unchanged": true,
+  "received_edition": "V1.0 R0;Family Documentation;Type Reference;Component Document Identity;Author Arnaldo Figueira;Canonical/Baseline1.0;English",
+  "explicit_advisory_statement": "Although the recommendations presented here are not normative requirements",
+  "coverage": "Complete15 chapters/36 numbered bodies;3 assignment/3 preservation/3 identifier/5 integration/7 anti-pattern headings;5 encoding examples/5 validation triggers/4 extension conditions/8 practice rows/11 specification contribution rows/11 dependencies;no diagrams orlocal constraint IDs;selected peers only",
+  "section_map": [
+    {
+      "number": "1",
+      "title": "Purpose",
+      "raw_heading": "# 1. Purpose",
+      "body": "\n\nThis document provides architectural best practices for the effective adoption and implementation of the **Document Identity** component.\n\nIts purpose is to recommend practices that preserve the architectural integrity, consistency, stability, and interoperability of document identities across all implementations of the Documentation Framework.\n\nThe recommendations contained in this document complement the normative specifications defined in the Architecture, Model, Schema, Validation, Governance, Relationships, Constraints, and Extensibility documents.\n\n---\n\n",
+      "body_sha256_utf8": "de604ca8d6de83450efbd1ee3518b7f4509d6f33096a6fec75e4ab0d9895a466"
+    },
+    {
+      "number": "2",
+      "title": "Introduction",
+      "raw_heading": "# 2. Introduction",
+      "body": "\n\nThe architectural specifications define **what** a Document Identity is and **which rules** it shall satisfy.\n\nThis document describes **recommended practices** for applying those specifications consistently.\n\nAlthough the recommendations presented here are not normative requirements, following them significantly improves interoperability, maintainability, traceability, and long-term architectural consistency.\n\n---\n\n",
+      "body_sha256_utf8": "8e4a6da6ceec602b1f503cc54c2f2b358ed14a2a7532f31afef3a0aaa7bdf8aa"
+    },
+    {
+      "number": "3",
+      "title": "General Recommendations",
+      "raw_heading": "# 3. General Recommendations",
+      "body": "\n\nImplementations should always treat Document Identity as a permanent architectural asset.\n\nDocument Identity should never be regarded as a technical identifier generated solely for implementation purposes.\n\nEvery implementation should preserve the canonical identity model defined by the Documentation Framework.\n\n---\n\n",
+      "body_sha256_utf8": "1f4283036e2d86be244bec44be43e466966abaedea17c7fb3c4423f980078d5f"
+    },
+    {
+      "number": "4",
+      "title": "Identity Assignment",
+      "raw_heading": "# 4. Identity Assignment",
+      "body": "\n\n",
+      "body_sha256_utf8": "75a11da44c802486bc6f65640aa48a730f0f684c5c07a42ba3cd1735eb3fb070"
+    },
+    {
+      "number": "4.1",
+      "title": "Assign Identity Once",
+      "raw_heading": "## 4.1. Assign Identity Once",
+      "body": "\n\nA Document Identity should be assigned only once during the architectural creation of a document.\n\nSubsequent document evolution should never generate a new identity.\n\n---\n\n",
+      "body_sha256_utf8": "33d3f3d64ce1969aaece4cc4091ad06162d1a29a9148d78855645736b02bef7f"
+    },
+    {
+      "number": "4.2",
+      "title": "Assign Identity Early",
+      "raw_heading": "## 4.2. Assign Identity Early",
+      "body": "\n\nWhenever possible, the identity should be established before the document enters governance processes.\n\nEarly identity assignment improves traceability throughout the document lifecycle.\n\n---\n\n",
+      "body_sha256_utf8": "bf5f5fcc527766bdd660fa2b1c6a947af58eb9b5ba46754141801978c1415986"
+    },
+    {
+      "number": "4.3",
+      "title": "Avoid Temporary Identities",
+      "raw_heading": "## 4.3. Avoid Temporary Identities",
+      "body": "\n\nTemporary or placeholder identifiers should be avoided.\n\nIf temporary identifiers are unavoidable, they should never become canonical Document Identities.\n\n---\n\n",
+      "body_sha256_utf8": "3e671418f0329936ea64d4d7a1cdf8ec9df5c444729100466d935903a797635e"
+    },
+    {
+      "number": "5",
+      "title": "Identity Preservation",
+      "raw_heading": "# 5. Identity Preservation",
+      "body": "\n\n",
+      "body_sha256_utf8": "75a11da44c802486bc6f65640aa48a730f0f684c5c07a42ba3cd1735eb3fb070"
+    },
+    {
+      "number": "5.1",
+      "title": "Preserve Identity During Revisions",
+      "raw_heading": "## 5.1. Preserve Identity During Revisions",
+      "body": "\n\nContent revisions, corrections, restructurings, or metadata updates should preserve the same Document Identity.\n\n---\n\n",
+      "body_sha256_utf8": "a4a710ea4f8f0c010bb757d5284016a9f8fa7e57094f9c44aa9eeb33bb3af23f"
+    },
+    {
+      "number": "5.2",
+      "title": "Preserve Identity During Migration",
+      "raw_heading": "## 5.2. Preserve Identity During Migration",
+      "body": "\n\nRepository migrations, storage migrations, and technology migrations should not affect document identity.\n\n---\n\n",
+      "body_sha256_utf8": "2e8404c7fcf356e3eee4cc041e6db3ec44d917b4f4ea158fb79550918dcd9537"
+    },
+    {
+      "number": "5.3",
+      "title": "Preserve Identity During Publication",
+      "raw_heading": "## 5.3. Preserve Identity During Publication",
+      "body": "\n\nPublishing documents in different formats should not create additional identities.\n\nA document possesses one canonical identity regardless of the number of published representations.\n\n---\n\n",
+      "body_sha256_utf8": "8335eb8741f24a1d8d030269aecec73a1849d78af357cdc72c24681491121fbc"
+    },
+    {
+      "number": "6",
+      "title": "Identifier Management",
+      "raw_heading": "# 6. Identifier Management",
+      "body": "\n\n",
+      "body_sha256_utf8": "75a11da44c802486bc6f65640aa48a730f0f684c5c07a42ba3cd1735eb3fb070"
+    },
+    {
+      "number": "6.1",
+      "title": "Prefer Stable Identifiers",
+      "raw_heading": "## 6.1. Prefer Stable Identifiers",
+      "body": "\n\nCanonical identifiers should remain stable throughout the complete lifetime of the document.\n\n---\n\n",
+      "body_sha256_utf8": "3dbb2f1577ec8ab7f4eaa8c1c5efa36c8bf98b58fd604eebee7a43b47a3f1c0b"
+    },
+    {
+      "number": "6.2",
+      "title": "Avoid Semantic Encoding",
+      "raw_heading": "## 6.2. Avoid Semantic Encoding",
+      "body": "\n\nIdentifiers should not embed information likely to change over time.\n\nExamples include:\n\n- repository names;\n- storage locations;\n- workflow states;\n- file paths;\n- implementation technologies.\n\nStable identifiers improve long-term maintainability.\n\n---\n\n",
+      "body_sha256_utf8": "1491245d3634f4c99ef1455a97f26861a2749f50c9755fdea683aa8f70cd91b5"
+    },
+    {
+      "number": "6.3",
+      "title": "Maintain Identifier Consistency",
+      "raw_heading": "## 6.3. Maintain Identifier Consistency",
+      "body": "\n\nEvery architectural reference should use the same canonical identifier.\n\nAlternative identifier representations should be treated only as implementation concerns.\n\n---\n\n",
+      "body_sha256_utf8": "3d775c9f01b4be67275a2a150e67ba4964b60f0fbf8eaab4d8bd251fa3fd382b"
+    },
+    {
+      "number": "7",
+      "title": "Cross-Component Integration",
+      "raw_heading": "# 7. Cross-Component Integration",
+      "body": "\n\n",
+      "body_sha256_utf8": "75a11da44c802486bc6f65640aa48a730f0f684c5c07a42ba3cd1735eb3fb070"
+    },
+    {
+      "number": "7.1",
+      "title": "Metadata",
+      "raw_heading": "## 7.1. Metadata",
+      "body": "\n\nMetadata should always reference an existing Document Identity.\n\nMetadata should never duplicate identity information.\n\n---\n\n",
+      "body_sha256_utf8": "d29286957e344a5e4a65524f65e3ce9b8640c5d2424d3b4bea2442bc6b73625d"
+    },
+    {
+      "number": "7.2",
+      "title": "Classification",
+      "raw_heading": "## 7.2. Classification",
+      "body": "\n\nClassification should categorise identified documents rather than defining document identities.\n\n---\n\n",
+      "body_sha256_utf8": "88f527c0aa80a28b37ca5087396b95af069c63924ba42621ac7c8aaf26c9bdfa"
+    },
+    {
+      "number": "7.3",
+      "title": "Registry",
+      "raw_heading": "## 7.3. Registry",
+      "body": "\n\nRegistry entries should reference canonical Document Identities.\n\nRegistry-specific identifiers should not replace canonical identities.\n\n---\n\n",
+      "body_sha256_utf8": "21b860d177a5a30a3783832bcb678165b50debdc06606fb60ce3a8bfe75f678d"
+    },
+    {
+      "number": "7.4",
+      "title": "Relationships",
+      "raw_heading": "## 7.4. Relationships",
+      "body": "\n\nRelationships should always be established between canonical Document Identities.\n\n---\n\n",
+      "body_sha256_utf8": "d179555f9237c326c0c41e9cfc6cccf018ed717b8f20baab745ba66566e18189"
+    },
+    {
+      "number": "7.5",
+      "title": "Knowledge Graph",
+      "raw_heading": "## 7.5. Knowledge Graph",
+      "body": "\n\nGraph nodes representing documents should preserve canonical identity semantics.\n\n---\n\n",
+      "body_sha256_utf8": "d43a8904735c228d3d0c83b13c793ed3364b4d223a96c5829456b4799ac82588"
+    },
+    {
+      "number": "8",
+      "title": "Governance Recommendations",
+      "raw_heading": "# 8. Governance Recommendations",
+      "body": "\n\nGovernance processes should preserve Document Identity throughout every operational state of the document.\n\nApproval workflows, reviews, publications, archival activities, and repository migrations should never modify document identities.\n\n---\n\n",
+      "body_sha256_utf8": "c5c22f0f945fdc2bf7e4c2e1332fbee5d8b402b4cb6ff51f9e7de0df5dffcba8"
+    },
+    {
+      "number": "9",
+      "title": "Validation Recommendations",
+      "raw_heading": "# 9. Validation Recommendations",
+      "body": "\n\nDocument Identity validation should be performed:\n\n- when assigning a new identity;\n- before document registration;\n- before publication;\n- during repository migration;\n- during consistency verification.\n\nRegular validation improves long-term architectural integrity.\n\n---\n\n",
+      "body_sha256_utf8": "8f7d8a99cba996ef8412e6986c8236b9315d79b15c5e02f3c992369dd1a6e1b7"
+    },
+    {
+      "number": "10",
+      "title": "Extensibility Recommendations",
+      "raw_heading": "# 10. Extensibility Recommendations",
+      "body": "\n\nFuture architectural extensions should:\n\n- preserve backward compatibility;\n- preserve canonical identity semantics;\n- preserve interoperability;\n- remain additive rather than destructive.\n\nExtensions should enrich the identity model without redefining its architectural meaning.\n\n---\n\n",
+      "body_sha256_utf8": "17ec77d481aa3f8297f14e3d1c86c1cee6a96af0b75a562821b1c1d6ffedf254"
+    },
+    {
+      "number": "11",
+      "title": "Common Anti-Patterns",
+      "raw_heading": "# 11. Common Anti-Patterns",
+      "body": "\n\nThe following practices should be avoided.\n\n",
+      "body_sha256_utf8": "517fe2c5df3054def2455a285d1a9f11ee29a6fd6ad65c80d84fb700acbf8df2"
+    },
+    {
+      "number": "11.1",
+      "title": "Multiple Identities",
+      "raw_heading": "## 11.1. Multiple Identities",
+      "body": "\n\nAssigning multiple identities to the same document.\n\n---\n\n",
+      "body_sha256_utf8": "f2e86a01d2a1781dc1ca5111d46101f842e8031b3d907f5e4fe6a8c12c23434b"
+    },
+    {
+      "number": "11.2",
+      "title": "Identity Reuse",
+      "raw_heading": "## 11.2. Identity Reuse",
+      "body": "\n\nReusing retired identities for new documents.\n\n---\n\n",
+      "body_sha256_utf8": "32db211544746be6c81a162336a92e308ae03fd8b2a76396eeb8b655875d2670"
+    },
+    {
+      "number": "11.3",
+      "title": "Mutable Identifiers",
+      "raw_heading": "## 11.3. Mutable Identifiers",
+      "body": "\n\nChanging identifiers after assignment.\n\n---\n\n",
+      "body_sha256_utf8": "04d39fc832756279608a9713960d71c86e12596d72fc87eedb74de2d60fa1556"
+    },
+    {
+      "number": "11.4",
+      "title": "Repository-Dependent Identities",
+      "raw_heading": "## 11.4. Repository-Dependent Identities",
+      "body": "\n\nDeriving identities from repository structures.\n\n---\n\n",
+      "body_sha256_utf8": "f90cc243da2a099e5e8ef1c5b6a3f7dfcfec245cf9ed2ee16cee3bbc95af7c2b"
+    },
+    {
+      "number": "11.5",
+      "title": "Technology-Dependent Identities",
+      "raw_heading": "## 11.5. Technology-Dependent Identities",
+      "body": "\n\nEmbedding implementation-specific information into canonical identifiers.\n\n---\n\n",
+      "body_sha256_utf8": "34a37699e8e7a3ca2ede3cce3f5813c168f60543ad803eeab489174442f161aa"
+    },
+    {
+      "number": "11.6",
+      "title": "Workflow-Dependent Identities",
+      "raw_heading": "## 11.6. Workflow-Dependent Identities",
+      "body": "\n\nChanging document identities according to workflow state.\n\n---\n\n",
+      "body_sha256_utf8": "b03cfa0e551a982c5e29bfd9271300f6125a52bf1ac274ad1d313bec03ccdfe9"
+    },
+    {
+      "number": "11.7",
+      "title": "Metadata-Derived Identities",
+      "raw_heading": "## 11.7. Metadata-Derived Identities",
+      "body": "\n\nGenerating identities from mutable metadata values.\n\n---\n\n",
+      "body_sha256_utf8": "e9852e1b68dcee5bc2f3eee4b7a0fcb06a68d01913d90fef57177958baa39ce8"
+    },
+    {
+      "number": "12",
+      "title": "Recommended Architectural Practices",
+      "raw_heading": "# 12. Recommended Architectural Practices",
