Identity Uniqueness | Preserve full qualified governing assignment/canonicalization contract with actual population/collision/history evidence |\n| Identity Immutability | Preserve assigned key/association; mutable support records retain their own responsible rules; necessary contract transition requires §9 |\n| Canonical Identity Model | Ordinary implementation extensions do not silently replace owner meaning; necessary normative/foundational revision requires actual prior/new authority/impact/version/transition assessment and visible peer reconciliation |\n\nDID-014§§7–8 mandatory State/Canonical Reference and DID-006 lifecycle authority remain actual owner work, not fields silently waived by these tables. No accepted merged model, Metadata Element/Profile, new domain, series, alias or allocation is created by an extensibility label.\n\n---\n\n"
