+          "text": "# 6. Extension Categories\n\nThe four original extension categories are conceptual groupings, not additional document Type values, registered components or automatic allocation to similarly named structural areas. Preserve their received titles, seven examples and actual owner/consumer boundaries. Examples indicate possible subjects, not implemented adapters or authorized operations.\n\n---\n\n## 6.1. Architectural Extensions\n\nArchitectural extensions introduce demonstrated concepts/contracts while preserving compatible meaning where feasible. The original example remains:\n\n- additional identity domains.\n\nNew domains require explicit governing authority, qualified semantics, canonical representation, allocation/reservation scope and affected consumer contracts. They are not a shortcut to renumber an existing document. For this corpus the domain is Documentation Framework, represented by DF; DF-SSS-NNN uses a registered uppercase three-letter stable allocation series and positive three-digit 001–999. 000 is not allocated; gaps prove no availability; allocated/retired numbers are not reused. At999, register a traceable unused continuation series rather than widen syntax or recycle. Current Family/Type/Component/path/status/edition does not reconstruct the key. Other domains require their own explicit contracts.\n\nA necessary change to an existing architectural contract is assessed under §9, not assumed harmless because it is called an additional domain. This UPDATE registers no domain/series and allocates no key.\n\n---\n\n## 6.2. Behavioural Extensions\n\nThe received heading Behavioural Extensions denotes additional validation/governance behavior, not a new normalized Type value. Its original example remains:\n\n- organisation-specific validation policies.\n\nActual responsible owners define applicable additional checks or policy conditions under common governing contracts. Record exact subject/rules/editions/context, authority/executor, performed checks, observations and coverage. DID-007 distinguishes Valid, Invalid, Inconsistent and Unresolvable; partial/unexecuted/missing/conflicting mandatory evidence cannot establish unconditional full validity or fabricated failure. An additional policy does not silently redefine mandatory semantics, create permissions ormerge unresolved State/Canonical Reference/lifecycle fields.\n\nDMS/tool/manual operation and CMS change scope are distinct from Workflow/Policies/Reviews/Baselines definitions. A result record or local PASS does not authorize allocation, correction, approval, publication orBaseline selection.\n\n---\n\n## 6.3. Integration Extensions\n\nIntegration extensions describe possible external exchange/adapter contracts. The two original examples remain:\n\n- external identifier mappings;\n- repository-specific adapters.\n\nMap intended qualified keys, canonical interpretations/aliases and exact editions/context with actual prior/new source/output provenance, owner authority and consumer compatibility. Repository locators and external strings are not automatically canonical document keys. Preserve reservations/history and immutable snapshot targets; no silent allocation, domain reassignment orretargeting is allowed.\n\nUse applicable registered Integration capabilities from ARC-005§9 when relevant:Source Control Integration, CI/CD Integration, IDE Integration, Documentation Platform Integration and AI Integration. The two examples are not new registered components orproof that any adapter exists. Actual execution requires applicable authorization, mappings, input/output editions/bytes, contributors, checks, observations and limits; generation/exchange cannot invent identity, state, approval orcontribution facts.\n\n---\n\n## 6.4. Implementation Extensions\n\nImplementation extensions realize applicable logical contracts without acquiring their semantic ownership. The three original examples remain:\n\n- programming language libraries;\n- database mappings;\n- API integrations.\n\nTheir implementation design remains outside this specification. That exclusion does not waive logical representation/interface, owner/authorization or evidence obligations. Actual implementations preserve intended qualified identity/edition/context, mappings/source provenance, contributors and applicable checks; storage/runtime choices are not proof of correctness orindependent consumer rollout.\n\nArchitectural capability, actual adapter/executor, generated output and observed result remain distinct. No language library, database model, API service, universal resolver orpermission model is supplied here.\n\n---\n\n"
